%S A123442 1,2,4,11,33,147,894,8515,120263,2363930,59986271,1892880962,
%T A123442 73518632639
%N A123442 Number of P_4-stable Berge perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123442 A graph is P_4-stable Berge if it is a Berge graph (no induced odd cycle of length at least 5 and no induced complement of one) that contains a stable set meeting every induced P_4 (path on 4 vertices); equivalently, deleting some stable set leaves a P_4-free graph (cograph). All such graphs are perfect. The class is closed under induced subgraphs. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 07 2026
%H A123442 S. Hougardy, <a href="http://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
